l methods and experiments in analytic number theory\u003C/em\u003E, Recent perspectives in random matrix theory and number theory, London Math. Soc. Lecture Note Ser., vol.\u0026nbsp;322, Cambridge Univ. Press, Cambridge, 2005, pp. 425\u0026ndash;506. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2166470\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E2166470\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511550492.015\u0022\u003E10.1017/CBO9780511550492.015\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Ze\u0026eacute;v Rudnick and Peter Sarnak, \u003Cem\u003EZeros of principal $L$-functions and random matrix theory\u003C/em\u003E, Duke Math. J. \u003Cstrong\u003E81\u003C/strong\u003E (1996), no. 2, 269\u0026ndash;322. A celebration of John F. Nash, Jr. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1395406\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E1395406\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1215/S0012-7094-96-08115-6\u0022\u003E10.1215/S0012-7094-96-08115-6\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Eric Saias and Andreas Weingartner, \u003Cem\u003EZeros of Dirichlet series with periodic coefficients\u003C/em\u003E, Acta Arith. \u003Cstrong\u003E140\u003C/strong\u003E (2009), no. 4, 335\u0026ndash;344. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2570109\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E2570109\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.4064/aa140-4-4\u0022\u003E10.4064/aa140-4-4\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Eero Saksman and Christian Webb, \u003Cem\u003EThe Riemann zeta function and Gaussian multiplicative chaos: statistics on the critical line\u003C/em\u003E, Ann. Probab. \u003Cstrong\u003E48\u003C/strong\u003E (2020), no. 6, 2680\u0026ndash;2754. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=4164452\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E4164452\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E