I \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01448042\u0022\u003E10.1007/BF01448042\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Norbert Tihanyi, \u003Cem\u003EFast method for locating peak values of the Riemann zeta function on the critical line\u003C/em\u003E, 2014 16th International Symposium on Symbolic and Numeric Algorithms for Scientific Computing IEEE; (2014) pp. 91-96.\n\u003Cli\u003E Norbert Tihanyi, Atilla Kov\u0026aacute;cs, and J\u0026oacute;zsef Kov\u0026aacute;cs, \u003Cem\u003EComputing extremely large values of the Riemann zeta function\u003C/em\u003E, J. Grid Computing \u003Cstrong\u003E15\u003C/strong\u003E (2017) pp. 527-534.\n\u003Cli\u003E E. C. Titchmarsh, \u003Cem\u003EThe theory of the Riemann zeta-function\u003C/em\u003E, 2nd ed., The Clarendon Press, Oxford University Press, New York, 1986. Edited and with a preface by D. R. Heath-Brown. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=882550\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E882550\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Timothy Trudgian, \u003Cem\u003EOn the success and failure of Gram\u0026rsquo;s law and the Rosser rule\u003C/em\u003E, Acta Arith. \u003Cstrong\u003E148\u003C/strong\u003E (2011), no. 3, 225\u0026ndash;256. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2794929\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E2794929\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.4064/aa148-3-2\u0022\u003E10.4064/aa148-3-2\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E","BibliographicInfo":"\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EDavid W. Farmer\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EAffiliation: American Institute of Mathematics, California Institute of Technology (Caltech) 8\u0026ndash;32, 1200 E California Blvd, Pasadena, California 91125\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EMR Author ID: \u003Ca href=\u0027https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?mrauthid=341467\u0027\u003E341467\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EORCID: \u003Ca href=\u0027https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9355-3389\u0027\u003E0000-0002-9355-3389\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EEmail: farmer@aimath.org\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EReceived by editor(s): December 8, 2022\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EReceived by editor(s) in revised form: April 13, 2025, and November 14, 2025\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EPublished electronically: August 12, 2026\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u0026copy; Copyright 2026\nAmerican Mathematical Society\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EJournal: Bull. Amer. Math. Soc. \u003Cstrong\u003E63\u003C/strong\u003E (2026), 559-636\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EMSC (2020): Primary 11M26, 11M50\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EDOI: https://doi.org/10.1090/bull/1890\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E","PdfUrl":"/2026-63-04/S0273-0979-2026-01890-5/S0273-0979-2026-01890-5.pdf","HtmlUrl":"/2026-63-04/S0273-0979-2026-01890-5/viewer","Authors":[{"RelationshipType":"AUTHOR","FullName":"David W. Farmer","FirstName":"David","MiddleName":"W.","LastName":"Farmer","Suffix":" ","MasterCustomerId":"FRDVWA","MRAuthorId":341467,"Email":"farmer@aimath.org","CustomerSequence":0,"Affiliation":"American Institute of Mathematics, California Institute of Technology (Caltech) 8\u0026ndash;32, 1200 E California Blvd, Pasadena, California 91125","AffiliationSequence":0,"FirstEditor":false,"Url":null,"Description":null,"BookReviewId":0,"CurrentAddress":null}],"BookReviews":[],"AMSCopyrightFlag":"Y","CopyrightOwner":"American Mathematical Society","MRNumber":null,"ArticleCitation":"Bull. Amer. Math. Soc. \u003Cstrong\u003E63\u003C/strong\u003E (2026), 559-636","CrossReferences":"","Abstracts":[],"IsAMSCopyright":true,"PostDateFormatted":"August 12, 2026"},{"ArticleId":93035,"JournalProductCode":"BULL","IssueId":5808,"ManuscriptId":1908,"DocumentType":"ARTICLE","Title":"Aspects of automatic continuity","DOI":"10.1090/bull/1908","PII":"S0273-0979-2026-01908-X","Issue":null,"IssueDirectory":"2026-63-04","StartPage":637,"EndPage":684,"PostDate":"2026-08-13T00:00:00","PrimaryMsc":"22A05","SecondaryMsc":"03E15, 03E25","MscSchema":"2020","Abstract":"A general overview of the phenomenon of automatic continuity of homomorphisms between Polish groups is given. In particular, we study variants and improvements of the closed graph theorem, applying these to the problem of continuity of universally measurable homomorphisms as well as to gauge the amount of choice needed to construct discontinuous homomorphisms between Polish groups. Furthermore, we provide a simple proof of automatic continuity in the context of homeomorphism groups of compact manifolds and a complete reworking of automatic continuity theory in the context of isometry groups of highly homogeneous complete metric structures.","EnhancedReferences":"\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Alperin%2C%20Roger\u0022\u003ERoger Alperin\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003ELocally compact groups acting on trees\u003C/em\u003E, Pacific J. Math. \u003Cstrong\u003E100\u003C/strong\u003E (1982), no.\u0026nbsp;1, 23\u0026ndash;32.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=661438\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E661438\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.2140/pjm.1982.100.23\u0022\u003E10.2140/pjm.1982.100.23\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Banakh%2C%20T.\u0022\u003ET. Banakh\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EAutomatic continuity of measurable homomorphisms on \u0026#x10C;ech-complete topological groups\u003C/em\u003E (2022).\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Ben%20Yaacov%2C%20Itai\u0022\u003EIta\u0026iuml; Ben Yaacov\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Berenstein%2C%20Alexander\u0022\u003EAlexander Berenstein\u003C/a\u003E, and \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Melleray%2C%20Julien\u0022\u003EJulien Melleray\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EPolish topometric groups\u003C/em\u003E, Trans. Amer. Math. Soc. \u003Cstrong\u003E365\u003C/strong\u003E (2013), no.\u0026nbsp;7, 3877\u0026ndash;3897.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=3042607\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E3042607\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9947-2013-05773-X\u0022\u003E10.1090/S0002-9947-2013-05773-X\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Bogopolski%2C%20Oleg\u0022\u003EOleg Bogopolski\u003C/a\u003E and \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Corson%2C%20Samuel%20M.\u0022\u003ESamuel M. Corson\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EAbstract homomorphisms from some topological groups to acylindrically hyperbolic groups\u003C/em\u003E, Math. Ann. \u003Cstrong\u003E384\u003C/strong\u003E (2022), no.\u0026nbsp;3-4, 1017\u0026ndash;1055.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=4498466\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E4498466\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1007/s00208-021-02278-4\u0022\u003E10.1007/s00208-021-02278-4\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Bochner%2C%20Salomon\u0022\u003ESalomon Bochner\u003C/a\u003E and \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Montgomery%2C%20Deane\u0022\u003EDeane Montgomery\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EGroups of differentiable and real or complex analytic transformations\u003C/em\u003E, An