ann zeta-function\u003C/em\u003E, Arch. Math. Naturvid. \u003Cstrong\u003E48\u003C/strong\u003E (1946), no. 5, 89\u0026ndash;155. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=20594\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E20594\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Atle Selberg, \u003Cem\u003EOld and new conjectures and results about a class of Dirichlet series\u003C/em\u003E, Proceedings of the Amalfi Conference on Analytic Number Theory (Maiori, 1989) Univ. Salerno, Salerno, 1992, pp. 367\u0026ndash;385. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1220477\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E1220477\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E O. Shanker, \u003Cem\u003EGood-to-bad Gram point ratio for Riemann zeta function\u003C/em\u003E, Exp. Math. \u003Cstrong\u003E30\u003C/strong\u003E (2021), no. 1, 76\u0026ndash;85. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=4223283\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E4223283\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1080/10586458.2018.1492474\u0022\u003E10.1080/10586458.2018.1492474\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Kannan Soundararajan, \u003Cem\u003EThe distribution of values of zeta and $L$-functions\u003C/em\u003E, ICM\u0026mdash;International Congress of Mathematicians. Vol. 2. Plenary lectures, EMS Press, Berlin, [2023] \u0026copy;2023, pp. 1260\u0026ndash;1310. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=4680281\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E4680281\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E Andreas Speiser, \u003Cem\u003EGeometrisches zur Riemannschen Zetafunktion\u003C/em\u003E, Math. Ann. \u003Cstrong\u003E110\u003C/strong\u003E (1935), no. 1, 514\u0026ndash;521 (German). \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1512953\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E1512953\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI 