class='productDetailTitle'>Jim Simons’ pure math research in the new millenium</div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Sullivan%2C%20Dennis' target='_blank'>Dennis Sullivan</a></div><div></div><li id='articleContent_91552' data-ams-pii='BULL1910'><div class='productDetailTitle'>Microlocal sheaf theory and symplectic geometry</div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Guillermou%2C%20St%5C%27ephane' target='_blank'>St&eacute;phane Guillermou</a></div><div></div><li id='articleContent_91553' data-ams-pii='BULL1909'><div class='productDetailTitle'>Quantum affine algebras and monoidal categorification of cluster algebras, after Kashiwara, Kim, Oh, and Park.</div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Leclerc%2C%20B.' target='_blank'>B. Leclerc</a></div><div></div><li id='articleContent_91555' data-ams-pii='BULL1911'><div class='productDetailTitle'>A celebration of Masaki Kashiwara</div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Schapira%2C%20Pierre' target='_blank'>Pierre Schapira</a></div><div></div><li id='articleContent_91712' data-ams-pii='BULL1912'><div class='productDetailTitle'>Mostow rigidity made easier</div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Schwartz%2C%20Richard' target='_blank'>Richard Evan Schwartz</a></div><div></div><li id='articleContent_91851' data-ams-pii='BULL1913'><div class='productDetailTitle'>The Kakeya conjecture: Where does it come from and why is it important?</div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Hickman%2C%20Jonathan' target='_blank'>Jonathan Hickman</a></div><div></div><li id='articleContent_91852' data-ams-pii='BULL1914'><div class='productDetailTitle'>A decades-long breakthrough in zero-density estimates and primes in short intervals</div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Turnage-Butterbaugh%2C%20Caroline' target='_blank'>Caroline L. Turnage-Butterbaugh</a></div><div></div><li id='articleContent_91864' data-ams-pii='BULL1915'><div class='productDetailTitle'>Problems on spherical maximal functions</div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Roos%2C%20Joris' target='_blank'>Joris Roos</a> and <a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Seeger%2C%20Andreas' target='_blank'>Andreas Seeger</a></div><div></div><li id='articleContent_91867' data-ams-pii='BULL1916'><div class='productDetailTitle'>Harmonic functions and random walks on groups written by Ariel Yadin</div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Saloff-Coste%2C%20Laurent' target='_blank'>Laurent Saloff-Coste</a></div><div></div><li id='articleContent_92380' data-ams-pii='BULL1917'><div class='productDetailTitle'>Trees of hyperbolic spaces written by Michael Kapovich and Pranab Sardar</div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Mj%2C%20Mahan' target='_blank'>Mahan Mj</a></div><div></div><li id='articleContent_92746' data-ams-pii='BULL1918'><div class='productDetailTitle'>Rank stability makes rings of integers diophantine</div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Poonen%2C%20Bjorn' target='_blank'>Bjorn Mikhail Poonen</a></div><div></div><li id='articleContent_92904' data-ams-pii='BULL1921'><div class='productDetailTitle'>First proof</div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Abouzaid%2C%20Mohammed' target='_blank'>Mohammed Abouzaid</a>, <a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Blumberg%2C%20Andrew' target='_blank'>Andrew J. Blumberg</a>, <a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Hairer%2C%20Martin' target='_blank'>Martin Hairer</a>, <a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Kileel%2C%20Joe' target='_blank'>Joe Kileel</a>, <a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Kolda%2C%20Tamara' target='_blank'>Tamara G. Kolda</a>, <a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Nelson%2C%20Paul' target='_blank'>Paul D. Nelson</a>, <a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Spielman%2C%20Daniel' target='_blank'>Daniel Spielman</a>, <a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Srivastava%2C%20Nikhil' target='_blank'>Nikhil Srivastava</a>, <a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Ward%2C%20Rachel' target='_blank'>Rachel Ward</a>, <a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Weinberger%2C%20Shmuel' target='_blank'>Shmuel Aaron Weinberger</a> and <a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Williams%2C%20Lauren' target='_blank'>Lauren Williams</a></div><div></div><li id='articleContent_92905' data-ams-pii='BULL1919'><div class='productDetailTitle'>Chaos in large genus surfaces</div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Arana-Herrera%2C%20Francisco' target='_blank'>Francisco Arana-Herrera</a></div><div></div><li id='articleContent_92906' data-ams-pii='BULL1920'><div class='productDetailTitle'>What is the geometric Langlands correspondence about?</div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Ben-Zvi%2C%20David' target='_blank'>David Ben-Zvi</a></div><div></div><li id='articleContent_93228' data-ams-pii='BULL1922'><div class='productDetailTitle'>Triangle covering problems and the Viterbo inequality in the plane</div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Balitskiy%2C%20Alexey' target='_blank'>Alexey Balitskiy</a>, <a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Mitrofanov%2C%20Ivan' target='_blank'>Ivan Mitrofanov</a> and <a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Polyanskii%2C%20Alexander' target='_blank'>Alexander Polyanskii</a></div><div></div><li id='articleContent_93487' data-ams-pii='BULL1923'><div class='productDetailTitle'>Quantum computation and quantum information–A mathematical perspective written by J. M. Landsberg</div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Kuperberg%2C%20Greg' target='_blank'>Greg Kuperberg</a></div><div></div><li id='articleContent_93718' data-ams-pii='BULL1924'><div class='productDetailTitle'>A spectral theory fo noncommuting operators written by Rongwei Yang</div><div><a href='https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/authors-search?query=Misra%2C%20Gadadhar' target='_blank'>Gadadhar Misra</a></div><div></div></ul></div>
